Split `styles.css` the way `volto-authomatic` splits its own: the root stylesheet now holds the design tokens and the handful of base classes more than one component wears, and everything that styles a single component lives in a `.scss` next to it, imported by that component. A rule is now found by opening the file whose markup it styles.

The base classes are worn explicitly — `identity-surface`, `identity-surface__header`, `identity-button`, `identity-button--danger`, `identity-note` — where they used to be selector lists naming every component that wanted the look, so a new component silently got none of it until somebody extended the list. Rules for markup that no longer exists went with the split, and the identities panel lost the card it was drawing inside the raised Segment its container already renders. @ericof
